<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoVariable - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/govariable/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/govariable/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 145</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_145/</link><pubDate>Sat, 28 Dec 2024 12:34:35 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_145/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;To define a package-level global string variable, which of the following syntax is correct (multiple choice):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. var str string&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. str := &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;D. var str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A, D&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Only &lt;code&gt;var&lt;/code&gt; can be used for global definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;B: Only supports local variable declaration.&#10;C: Assignment, not definition.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 053</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_053/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:33 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_053/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;To define a package-level global string variable, which of the following syntax is correct (multiple choice):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A. var str string&#10;B. str := &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&#10;C. str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&#10;D. var str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A, D&#10;The key is &amp;ldquo;package-level global&amp;rdquo;.&#10;B: &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; can only be used inside functions.&#10;C: This is an assignment, not a declaration.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>